-- title:
--   Level automorphisms act transitively on branches below a supersingular point
-- statement:
--   Arithmetic data. Throughout, $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ are primes with $\ell\ne q$, and $M'\ne 0$ is a natural number divisible neither by $q$ (`hqM'`) nor by $\ell$ (`hℓM'`). $L$ is a field of characteristic zero, $\xi\in L$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and `hι` requires a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. The field $K$ is an intermediate field of $L\subseteq\operatorname{LaurentSeries}(L)$, pinned by `hK` to be [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103): the $L$-subfield of $\operatorname{LaurentSeries}(L)$ generated by the image under the coefficient embedding $\operatorname{LaurentSeries}(\mathbb Q)\to\operatorname{LaurentSeries}(L)$ of the $q$-expansion function field of level $\mathrm{Gamma}_H$ with $N_0=(q\ell)^2M'$ and $H=$ `levelH (q*ℓ) M'`, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/N_0)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   The base ring $A$ is a henselian discrete valuation domain with an algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ its fraction field, with algebraically closed residue field, with $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`), with $\xi$ in the image of $A$ (`hξA`), and with a uniformiser $\varpi$ (`hϖ`: $\mathfrak m_A=(\varpi)$); $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. The element $j\in K$ is nonzero and its Laurent series is the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant (`hj`). The element $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Write $C=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, and `jChartFin A ↥K j` for $j$ regarded in $C$. The ideal $y\subset C$ is maximal and contains $\varpi$ (`hy`, `hϖy`), and `hss` requires that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of $j\in\Omega$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that invariant has no nonzero point annihilated by $q$.
--
--   The rigidity hypothesis `hArig`. For every point $z$ of the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak X=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout of the two chart spectra), every germ $\varpi_z$ at $z$ of the global section of $\mathfrak X$ obtained from $\varpi$ along `toBase` (`hϖz`) lying in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ (`hz`), and every point $y'$ of `XFin A ↥K j` $=\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin` mapping $y'$ to $z$ (`hy'`) and satisfying the same supersingularity condition at $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ as `hss` (`hss'`), there exist: an adically complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma:A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f-(X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1)\in(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (so $f$ agrees to order $q+1$ with [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion $\widehat{\mathcal O}_{\mathfrak X,z}$ onto $S=W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v-fu)$, such that seven clauses hold, stated with $\mathrm{toC}$ the completion map, $\mathrm{mkS}$ the quotient map onto $S$, and $\mathrm{germY}:C\to\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ the canonical map through the chart: (A1) for $a\in A$ the image of $a$ in $\widehat{\mathcal O}_{\mathfrak X,z}$ is carried by $e$ to $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma a))$; (A2) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau\in K\simeq_L K$ with `IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ` — that is, $\tau$ realises on ratios $f_1/f_2$ of modular forms of level $\mathrm{Gamma}_H$ with integral $q$-expansions, read in $\mathbb C$ through any $\iota$ sending $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, the slash action of the conjugated matrix `conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹` — the automorphism $\tau$ maps $C$ into $C$; (A3) if moreover $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$ then the restriction of such a $\tau$ to $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$; (A4) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, such a $\tau$ preserving $C$ and congruent to the identity modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W)$ with: $\theta\circ e\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}=e\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}\circ\tau$ on $C$; $\theta$ fixing the constants $\mathrm{mkS}(C(w))$; $\theta(\mathrm{mkS}(X_j))\equiv\sum_i\mathrm{mkS}(C(M_{ij})X_i)$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0),\mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$; $c^{q+1}\equiv1$, $M_{ij}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$; $c\equiv1$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$; and $c-1\notin\mathfrak m_W$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; (A5) branch separation: for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and prime ideals $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each omitting at least one of $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0),\mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$, each containing $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma\varpi))$, and each containing some $\mathrm{mkS}(C(a_i)X_0+C(b_i)X_1+h)$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ to $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ along $e\circ\mathrm{toC}$ are distinct; (A6) for a prime $P$ of $S$ omitting one of $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0),\mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$, containing $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma\varpi))$ and containing some $\mathrm{mkS}(C(1)X_0+C(0)X_1+h)$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$: an element $a\in C$ has $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(a))$ in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$; (A7) an Igusa-type normalisation of $j$: the series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the $q$-expansion of $j$ with all exponents multiplied by $q\ell$) lies in $K$ and in $C$, there is $a_0\in A$ with the difference of the two in $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, and there are $e_0\ge1$ and $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that for all $a,b\in W$ not both in $\mathfrak m_W$ with $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_W$ the form $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0}\mathrm{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{\,e_0-i}$ is a unit, and $e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(\,\cdot\,-a_0)))=\mathrm{mkS}(h)$ for that element.
--
--   A fixed chart at $y$. Data $z,\varpi_z,y'$ as above are fixed, with $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}=y$ (`hy'y`), together with one witness $W_1,\sigma_1,f_1,u_1,v_1,e_1$ of the same shape (complete discrete valuation domain, $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$, $u_1,v_1$ units, $f_1$ agreeing with the Drinfeld form to order $q+1$, and $e_1$ an isomorphism of $\widehat{\mathcal O}_{\mathfrak X,z}$ with $S_1=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1-f_1u_1)$), and the hypothesis `hW₁` asserting for this witness exactly the seven clauses (A1)–(A7) listed above.
--
--   The centre ideal, the blown-up algebra and the valuation subring. The ideal $J\subseteq C$ is pinned by `hJ` to be the infimum of the ideals obtained as follows: for $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism for $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$, take the contraction along $e_1\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}$ of the ideal of $S_1$ generated by $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)),\mathrm{mkS}(X_0),\mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$, and then its preimage under the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$. The $A$-subalgebra $B\subseteq K$ is pinned by `hB` to be the $C$-algebra generated by $\{x\in K:\ x\varpi_t\in J\}$, that is $B=C[J/\varpi_t]$. Furthermore $W$ is a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`), and four further hypothesis blocks are imposed: `hR1`, that $C\le B$ and every $f\in K$ is a ratio $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\ne0$; `hR2`, that $A\to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and $B/(\varpi)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses), that $W\cap L=A$, that $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that for $b\in C$ one has $b\in y$ if and only if $b$ lies in $\mathfrak m_W$, and that $W$ consists of the ratios $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $h\notin\mathfrak m_W$; and `hEQ` (five clauses), that for every $\mathrm{GaloisField}\ q\ 2$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho:B\to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) $=k[X_0,X_1]/(\mathrm{drinfeldPoly}-1)$ whose kernel is $B\cap\mathfrak m_W$, which is compatible with $A\to k$, and which intertwines each level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and preserving $W$ with the action `hAction q k` of an element $(\mathrm{redQ}\ q\ \gamma,c)$ of the subgroup `hSubgroup q`, with $c\ne1$ whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\ne\mathrm{id}$; that level automorphisms attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserve $B$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ contains the image under some level automorphism attached to some $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ of all elements of $B\cap\mathfrak m_W$; that an element of $B$ all of whose translates under level automorphisms attached to elements of $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ lie in $\mathfrak m_W$ is divisible by $\varpi$ in $B$; and that a level automorphism attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserves $W$ as soon as it preserves $y$.
--
--   Conclusion. For all ideals $\mathfrak p,\mathfrak p'$ of $C$ such that $\mathfrak p$ is prime, contains $\varpi$, satisfies $\mathfrak p\le y$ and $\mathfrak p\ne y$, and likewise for $\mathfrak p'$, there exist $\gamma\in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ with `IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ` such that: for all $f\in K$, $f\in W$ if and only if $\tau f\in W$; for all $a\in K$ with $a\in C$ one has $\tau a\in C$; and for every $c\in C$ and every proof that $\tau c\in C$, $c\in\mathfrak p$ if and only if $\tau c\in\mathfrak p'$. Thus one single level automorphism, preserving the valuation subring $W$ and the chart algebra $C$, carries $\mathfrak p'$ back to $\mathfrak p$.
--
--   This is the transitivity statement for the geometric action on the branches of the special fibre through a supersingular point: the primes of the $j$-finite chart algebra lying strictly below the supersingular maximal ideal $y$ and containing the uniformiser are permuted transitively by the automorphisms of the function field attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$, via automorphisms that respect both the chart algebra and the valuation subring $W$. It feeds the construction of the finite set of ends and of the localisation of the blow-up chart in the analysis of the supersingular points of the modular curve of level $(q\ell)^2M'$.
